# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python reconstruction service (soleiq-web/soleiq-foot-ai)
#
# The SOURCE is tracked — it is part of the product and belongs under review.
# Excluded is everything enormous, machine-specific, or protected:
#
#   local-data/  patient scan videos and extracted frames. PHI. Never commit.
#   .venv/       1.8GB, and a venv bakes in absolute paths, so it is not
#                portable between machines anyway. Rebuild it, never copy it.
#   artifacts/   trained weights and FAISS indexes, ~180MB, regenerated by
#                `make train` / `make build-similarity-index`.
#   data/        datasets, several carrying their own licence terms. Note this
#                is the TOP-LEVEL data/ only — src/data/ is source and tracked.
#   .env         API keys.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
soleiq-web/soleiq-foot-ai/local-data/
soleiq-web/soleiq-foot-ai/.venv/
soleiq-web/soleiq-foot-ai/artifacts/
soleiq-web/soleiq-foot-ai/data/
soleiq-web/soleiq-foot-ai/.env
soleiq-web/soleiq-foot-ai/env./
soleiq-web/soleiq-foot-ai/**/__pycache__/
soleiq-web/soleiq-foot-ai/**/.pytest_cache/

# The old standalone copy, renamed aside when the service moved in. 1.3GB and
# stale — safe to delete, but it must not become 1.3GB of tracked files first.
# Leading slash so these match at the repo root ONLY and cannot swallow the
# real service nested under soleiq-web/.
/soleiq-foot-ai/
/soleiq-foot-ai.superseded-*/
